<i>♪ When all I've ever learned</i>
<i>Is how to lie ♪</i>

1224
01:02:15,336 --> 01:02:18,707
<i>♪ Well, the hidden hands</i>
<i>Of wisdom ♪</i>

1225
01:02:18,806 --> 01:02:23,043
<i>♪ Holds all that</i>
<i>It can keep... ♪</i>

1226
01:02:25,879 --> 01:02:27,515
[in Spanish]

1227
01:02:31,118 --> 01:02:35,055
[in English] Uh... English.
Sorry, I don't speak <i>español.</i>

1228
01:02:35,155 --> 01:02:37,391
Everyone on the deck! Now!

1229
01:02:37,491 --> 01:02:40,494
What...? What seems to be
the problem, officer?

1230
01:02:42,062 --> 01:02:44,633
Are these all the passengers?

1231
01:02:44,733 --> 01:02:46,601
Yeah. That's it.

1232
01:02:46,701 --> 01:02:48,670
Do you have
a Tatiana Scott on board?

1233
01:02:48,769 --> 01:02:51,405
No, no. Just us <i>hombres.</i>

1234
01:02:51,506 --> 01:02:53,841
Do you recognize her?

1235
01:02:55,276 --> 01:02:59,046
Yeah, I believe she was
on our last tour.

1236
01:02:59,146 --> 01:03:01,583
-Why?
-We received an SOS signal

1237
01:03:01,683 --> 01:03:02,950
from her phone.

1238
01:03:03,050 --> 01:03:05,152
The ping was in this location.

1239
01:03:05,252 --> 01:03:06,186
Uh...

1240
01:03:07,821 --> 01:03:10,457
-Is she American?
-That's right. Yeah.

1241
01:03:10,558 --> 01:03:15,029
I recall her losing her phone
while she was in the cage.

1242
01:03:17,064 --> 01:03:18,600
Mind if we look around?

1243
01:03:18,700 --> 01:03:20,901
No, no. Go ahead. Yeah.

1244
01:03:27,542 --> 01:03:28,576
[in Spanish]

1245
01:03:41,121 --> 01:03:42,956
[Kayle]
You think that's the police?

1246
01:03:43,057 --> 01:03:46,628
It has to be.
Otherwise, why would they stop?

1247
01:03:47,461 --> 01:03:51,198
Can somebody hear us? Hello?
Hey! Hi! We're down here.

1248
01:03:55,670 --> 01:03:57,037
Where's your shark cage?

1249
01:03:57,137 --> 01:04:00,107
Oh, I'm in the process
of getting a new one.

1250
01:04:00,207 --> 01:04:02,744
You know, safety protocols
and whatnot.

1251
01:04:02,843 --> 01:04:04,311
Yours wasn't safe?

1252
01:04:04,411 --> 01:04:07,448
No, no, just routine
maintenance, you know?

1253
01:04:09,483 --> 01:04:12,219
Why aren't they answering us?
We're down here!

1254
01:04:12,319 --> 01:04:15,089
Kayle, you have to calm down.

1255
01:04:15,189 --> 01:04:16,758
I think I'm being
extremely calm,

1256
01:04:16,857 --> 01:04:18,693
considering
the circumstances, T.

1257
01:04:18,793 --> 01:04:20,795
Hey, remember what I told you:

1258
01:04:20,894 --> 01:04:23,097
breathe slow and keep pressure
on that arm.

1259
01:04:23,197 --> 01:04:25,132
Okay, but we have to head up.

1260
01:04:25,232 --> 01:04:27,635
-We should just go for it.
-Yeah.

1261
01:04:27,736 --> 01:04:29,503
You gotta give me
another minute.

1262
01:04:29,604 --> 01:04:32,841
I really need these sharks
to leave first, please.

1263
01:04:32,940 --> 01:04:36,243
-T, I'm gonna try.
-No, not with your arm.

1264
01:04:36,343 --> 01:04:38,847
-I can make it.
-Let's just wait.

1265
01:04:39,279 --> 01:04:41,315
Kyle's body is still up there.

1266
01:04:41,415 --> 01:04:44,451
Maybe they'll find him, and then
they'll have to look for us.

1267
01:04:45,620 --> 01:04:46,954
[officer 1 in Spanish]

1268
01:04:50,290 --> 01:04:51,959
[in English] Are you married?

1269
01:04:56,930 --> 01:04:58,999
Yes.

1270
01:04:59,099 --> 01:05:02,369
-Do you have kids?
-Yes, I have kids.

1271
01:05:03,904 --> 01:05:06,641
There's nothing like family.

1272
01:05:11,145 --> 01:05:13,581
There's nothing like family.

1273
01:05:14,749 --> 01:05:15,983
It's for them.

1274
01:05:19,153 --> 01:05:20,822
[officer 2] I checked
Tatiana's social media.

1275
01:05:20,921 --> 01:05:22,990
She posted a picture
this morning,

1276
01:05:23,090 --> 01:05:24,992
getting ready
to go shark diving.

1277
01:05:25,092 --> 01:05:28,763
Well, like I said, you know,
she was on my last tour,

1278
01:05:28,863 --> 01:05:30,698
lost her phone
and I dropped them off.

1279
01:05:30,799 --> 01:05:34,435
But I thought you said
you were getting a new cage.

1280
01:05:34,536 --> 01:05:38,706
Yeah, I got rid of the old one
this morning.

1281
01:05:38,807 --> 01:05:40,107
Everything is good below.

1282
01:05:40,508 --> 01:05:42,777
Let's let these men
finish their party.

1283
01:05:42,877 --> 01:05:44,945
But I have a few more questions.

1284
01:05:45,045 --> 01:05:46,113
[in Spanish]

1285
01:05:48,015 --> 01:05:49,483
[Kayle] <i>This is taking too long.</i>

1286
01:05:49,584 --> 01:05:54,021
I'm gonna try. I'm sorry, T.
I can't miss my only chance.

1287
01:05:54,121 --> 01:05:55,956
<i>-Kayle!</i>
-It's fine.

1288
01:05:56,056 --> 01:05:59,993
-I'm going up.
<i>-Kayle, stay where you are.</i>

1289
01:06:00,728 --> 01:06:02,262
Hello?

1290
01:06:03,598 --> 01:06:05,232
Shit!

1291
01:06:05,867 --> 01:06:08,837
Damn it!
Kayle, get back in the cage!

1292
01:06:08,937 --> 01:06:10,237
<i>I can't see the sharks.</i>

1293
01:06:10,337 --> 01:06:13,207
Seriously, they could be
headed toward you.

1294
01:06:13,307 --> 01:06:16,878
<i>Answer me, Kayle! Damn it!</i>

1295
01:06:16,977 --> 01:06:18,378
[creaking]

1296
01:06:19,681 --> 01:06:21,649
<i>Please, please,</i>
<i>just stay in the cage.</i>

1297
01:06:21,749 --> 01:06:26,487
<i>Just... God! Kayle,</i>
<i>we have to go up together.</i>

1298
01:06:26,588 --> 01:06:29,591
<i>Can you answer me, please?</i>
<i>Can you hear me?</i>

1299
01:06:29,691 --> 01:06:32,794
The BCD isn't working.
It isn't taking me up.

1300
01:06:32,894 --> 01:06:34,929
-Come on.
<i>-The pressure is too low.</i>

1301
01:06:35,028 --> 01:06:37,231
<i>Just stay where you are.</i>

1302
01:06:37,899 --> 01:06:40,200
<i>Oh my God, Kayle.</i>

1303
01:06:40,935 --> 01:06:42,002
<i>Hold on.</i>

1304
01:06:42,102 --> 01:06:44,238
[ominous music playing]

1305
01:06:45,172 --> 01:06:46,340
[Kayle screams]

1306
01:06:46,440 --> 01:06:49,911
-Oh! Shit!
-Oh my God! [yells]

1307
01:06:50,010 --> 01:06:53,548
-[whimpering]
-Kayle, what just happened?

1308
01:06:53,648 --> 01:06:56,350
[breathes shakily] My leg.

1309
01:06:56,450 --> 01:06:58,620
<i>Kayle, it's okay, it's okay.</i>

1310
01:07:01,255 --> 01:07:03,892
<i>Kayle, what is going on?</i>

1311
01:07:03,992 --> 01:07:05,459
[Kayle whimpers]

1312
01:07:05,560 --> 01:07:07,962
Listen, I need you to tell me
what is happening.

1313
01:07:08,061 --> 01:07:11,498
-What's wrong? Kayle!
-[whimpering]

1314
01:07:11,599 --> 01:07:14,201
[sobbing]

1315
01:07:17,805 --> 01:07:18,940
<i>Kayle.</i>

1316
01:07:19,039 --> 01:07:20,875
I'm in the cage!
I'm in the cage!

1317
01:07:20,975 --> 01:07:22,577
<i>-Okay, that's good.</i>
-Okay.

1318
01:07:22,677 --> 01:07:27,314
Just... Just stay calm.
Let me think. Let me think.

1319
01:07:27,414 --> 01:07:29,249
You have a tourniquet
on your vest?

1320
01:07:29,349 --> 01:07:31,051
-There's a lot of blood.
-I know.

1321
01:07:31,151 --> 01:07:34,154
Just use that to stop
the bleeding, okay?

1322
01:07:34,789 --> 01:07:38,225
<i>It's gonna be okay.</i>
<i>Just put it above the wound.</i>

1323
01:07:38,325 --> 01:07:40,127
And watch your breathing, okay?

1324
01:07:40,227 --> 01:07:41,930
You're using up all your oxygen.

1325
01:07:42,030 --> 01:07:44,464
[whimpers]
I'm losing a lot of blood.

1326
01:07:44,566 --> 01:07:46,935
<i>I know, but you've gotta</i>
<i>pull it tight. Come on.</i>

1327
01:07:47,035 --> 01:07:48,168
[screams]

1328
01:07:48,670 --> 01:07:49,704
[Burns] Hey.

1329
01:07:49,871 --> 01:07:51,773
Please understand that
I'm gonna check their hotel.

1330
01:07:51,873 --> 01:07:54,776
If they aren't there, I will
continue this investigation.

1331
01:07:54,876 --> 01:07:59,346
And if I can't locate Tatiana
Scott or any of her friends,

1332
01:07:59,446 --> 01:08:01,381
expect a new visit from me.

1333
01:08:02,115 --> 01:08:04,151
-All right.
-Morales!

1334
01:08:09,089 --> 01:08:11,659
Well, I hope you find them.

1335
01:08:14,028 --> 01:08:16,965
-[Tatiana] Are they leaving?
-[Kayle] <i>No, they can't leave.</i>

1336
01:08:17,065 --> 01:08:18,465
<i>They can't leave.</i>

1337
01:08:19,067 --> 01:08:20,500
No, no, no, no!

1338
01:08:20,602 --> 01:08:24,271
They can't leave us.
They can't leave us.

1339
01:08:24,371 --> 01:08:26,874
They're not gonna leave us.

1340
01:08:26,975 --> 01:08:30,044
I got an idea. [panting]

1341
01:08:30,143 --> 01:08:32,479
I'm sending
the creepy smoker up.

1342
01:08:32,580 --> 01:08:34,716
[groans]

1343
01:08:38,452 --> 01:08:41,756
Kayle, I'm heading back to you.

1344
01:08:42,690 --> 01:08:44,424
Just hold on.

1345
01:08:57,839 --> 01:08:58,673
[in Spanish]

1346
01:09:03,210 --> 01:09:04,779
[Kayle whimpering]

1347
01:09:04,879 --> 01:09:05,847
-Kayle!
-[gasps]

1348
01:09:05,947 --> 01:09:10,150
Kayle! I'm here, I'm here.
It's gonna be okay.

1349
01:09:10,250 --> 01:09:13,021
-Oh my God!
-[continues whimpering]

1350
01:09:13,121 --> 01:09:15,455
Oh my God.
There's so much blood.

1351
01:09:15,556 --> 01:09:17,625
-Oh my God.
-[breathes shakily]

1352
01:09:17,725 --> 01:09:19,393
We need to get you
to the surface.

1353
01:09:19,493 --> 01:09:20,561
I'm not sure I can swim.

1354
01:09:20,962 --> 01:09:24,599
I'm so sorry, Kayle,
but the police are leaving.

1355
01:09:24,699 --> 01:09:27,902
We need to get you up.
We don't have much time.

1356
01:09:28,002 --> 01:09:29,804
We need to get moving.

1357
01:09:29,904 --> 01:09:31,371
[police siren blaring]

1358
01:09:36,209 --> 01:09:37,645
Well?

1359
01:09:39,080 --> 01:09:40,313
Oh, shit.

1360
01:09:40,414 --> 01:09:44,986
Hey, I've got you.
Okay? I've got you.

1361
01:09:45,086 --> 01:09:47,055
-[whimpering]
-Just keep going.

1362
01:09:47,155 --> 01:09:49,924
-[groaning]
-We're almost there.

1363
01:09:51,291 --> 01:09:52,359
[in Spanish]

1364
01:09:54,128 --> 01:09:55,730
[groaning]

1365
01:09:55,830 --> 01:09:58,800
Martin. Martin. Martin.

1366
01:09:58,900 --> 01:10:00,233
[both groaning]

1367
01:10:02,170 --> 01:10:05,673
[Kayle whimpering]

1368
01:10:06,941 --> 01:10:07,775
Help!

1369
01:10:08,308 --> 01:10:09,242
[in Spanish]

1370
01:10:09,644 --> 01:10:12,814
-[gasps for air]
-Help! She's hurt! Help!

1371
01:10:14,849 --> 01:10:16,416
-Help!
-Morales!

1372
01:10:16,517 --> 01:10:18,820
-[Kayle whimpers]
-Hey!

1373
01:10:18,920 --> 01:10:19,721
Well, we're fucked.

1374
01:10:19,821 --> 01:10:23,457
-Come on!
-Help! She's hurt! Help us!

1375
01:10:23,558 --> 01:10:25,292
[officer 1 in Spanish]
Hey, come here!

1376
01:10:25,392 --> 01:10:27,360
-What are you smiling at?
-[indistinct yelling]

1377
01:10:27,461 --> 01:10:30,832
Help! Help us! Here!

1378
01:10:30,932 --> 01:10:32,232
[in Spanish]

1379
01:10:34,969 --> 01:10:37,437
[indistinct yelling]

1380
01:10:40,208 --> 01:10:41,642
[yelling indistinctly]

1381
01:10:43,911 --> 01:10:45,378
[Tatiana] Here!

1382
01:10:45,479 --> 01:10:46,313
[in Spanish] Come on!

1383
01:10:46,413 --> 01:10:48,716
-[Kayle] Help!
-Delgado! Now!

1384
01:10:49,382 --> 01:10:51,318
[rapid gunshots]

1385
01:10:52,252 --> 01:10:54,188
-Nice.
-Morales!

1386
01:10:54,287 --> 01:10:55,355
[choking]

1387
01:11:01,294 --> 01:11:03,330
Keep going, keep going.

1388
01:11:05,800 --> 01:11:07,501
[gunshots]

1389
01:11:13,908 --> 01:11:15,109
Wow!

1390
01:11:15,209 --> 01:11:17,678
[both screaming, muttering]

1391
01:11:17,779 --> 01:11:21,115
-Holy shit! Holy shit!
-[Burns laughing]

1392
01:11:21,215 --> 01:11:22,617
That was amazing, Delgado!

1393
01:11:22,717 --> 01:11:25,186
Burns, what the hell
are you doing?

1394
01:11:25,285 --> 01:11:26,386
That was fantastic, isn't it?

1395
01:11:26,486 --> 01:11:28,523
You can't blow up
a bloody police boat.

1396
01:11:28,623 --> 01:11:30,925
I can blow up whatever I want.

1397
01:11:31,025 --> 01:11:34,996
Keep running your mouth
and your boat is next.

1398
01:11:35,897 --> 01:11:36,964
[whimpers]

1399
01:11:37,064 --> 01:11:38,966
You're okay. Hold me.
Hold on. You're okay.

1400
01:11:39,066 --> 01:11:42,770
It's okay, Kayle, it's okay.
Come on, come on.

1401
01:11:42,870 --> 01:11:44,705
Any sign of Martin?

1402
01:11:45,273 --> 01:11:47,775
What was left of him
was on that boat.

1403
01:11:48,709 --> 01:11:51,145
I am not leaving without my bag.

1404
01:11:51,245 --> 01:11:55,183
-[Kayle screams]
-Hold me, hold me.

1405
01:11:55,283 --> 01:11:57,852
[whimpering]

1406
01:11:57,952 --> 01:12:00,955
-[Kayle whimpering]
-Hold on. [grunts]

1407
01:12:01,055 --> 01:12:02,223
[whimpering]

1408
01:12:02,322 --> 01:12:05,059
Finally. Yeah! We meet properly.

1409
01:12:05,159 --> 01:12:06,794
Don't just stand there.
Help her!

1410
01:12:06,894 --> 01:12:10,363
You heard the lady.
Help her, come on.

1411
01:12:10,463 --> 01:12:13,267
[Kayle crying]

1412
01:12:13,366 --> 01:12:15,136
You have to be careful.

1413
01:12:15,236 --> 01:12:18,573
[Kayle yelling]

1414
01:12:20,308 --> 01:12:22,910
-[Tatiana] Careful!
-[breathing shakily]

1415
01:12:23,010 --> 01:12:26,047
-Kayle, it's okay, it's okay.
-[groaning]

1416
01:12:26,147 --> 01:12:27,682
-[screams]
-[Tatiana] Careful!

1417
01:12:27,782 --> 01:12:30,084
I know it hurts,
just stay awake.

1418
01:12:30,184 --> 01:12:31,686
Please, Kayle! Kayle!

1419
01:12:31,786 --> 01:12:33,754
Can somebody find
a first aid kit?

1420
01:12:34,755 --> 01:12:36,824
Help me, please!
Or she's gonna die.

1421
01:12:37,357 --> 01:12:39,160
It's okay. It's okay. It's okay.

1422
01:12:39,260 --> 01:12:41,128
Oh my God. Oh my God.

1423
01:12:41,229 --> 01:12:42,864
-My God!
-[Kayle screams]

1424
01:12:42,964 --> 01:12:44,332
[Logan] I need you
to release this tourniquet

1425
01:12:44,431 --> 01:12:46,366
every 15 minutes, all right?

1426
01:12:46,466 --> 01:12:48,236
And keep that leg elevated.

1427
01:12:48,336 --> 01:12:50,171
-It's okay, Kayle.
-Keep it warm.

1428
01:12:50,271 --> 01:12:51,138
We got her, we got her.

1429
01:12:51,239 --> 01:12:54,609
-Okay, okay.
-There you go.

1430
01:12:54,709 --> 01:12:57,178
-Hey, hey.
-She's lost a lot of blood.

1431
01:12:57,278 --> 01:12:58,613
We need to get her
to a hospital.

1432
01:12:58,713 --> 01:13:01,481
Yeah, yeah.
You heard that, Tatiana?

1433
01:13:01,582 --> 01:13:03,751
If you want your friend
to leave,

1434
01:13:03,851 --> 01:13:05,887
you better deliver
on your end of our deal.

1435
01:13:05,987 --> 01:13:11,525
You know, I mean, my bag
and this will all be over, eh?

1436
01:13:15,563 --> 01:13:17,665
-I won't.
-Hey. What?

1437
01:13:17,765 --> 01:13:20,701
-I can't.
-You can! I know you can!

1438
01:13:20,801 --> 01:13:23,304
Damn it, Burns,
I told you I'd go!

1439
01:13:23,403 --> 01:13:25,706
I know this shark!
It's a man-eater!

1440
01:13:25,806 --> 01:13:28,976
The girl was lucky once,
all right? Let me go.

1441
01:13:29,076 --> 01:13:31,478
-I'll get your goods.
-[Burns] No, you won't!

1442
01:13:31,579 --> 01:13:33,581
This is between her and me.

1443
01:13:33,681 --> 01:13:37,285
Okay? So now sit down
or I will kill you,

1444
01:13:37,385 --> 01:13:38,552
burn your boat,

1445
01:13:38,653 --> 01:13:41,822
murder your son
and never think about you again!

1446
01:13:45,293 --> 01:13:47,828
So, listen, Tatiana. Yeah.

1447
01:13:47,929 --> 01:13:52,366
I have been
extremely patient with you,

1448
01:13:52,465 --> 01:13:54,869
and I don't like
to make things personal.

1449
01:13:54,969 --> 01:13:57,305
But you have left me
no other choice.

1450
01:13:57,405 --> 01:14:02,209
And I understand
you two know each other.

1451
01:14:02,310 --> 01:14:04,545
-T! T!
-Kyle! Kyle!

1452
01:14:04,645 --> 01:14:06,614
Please, let me up.
Wait! Let me up!

1453
01:14:06,714 --> 01:14:10,051
No, no. Stay there. No, no, no.
Until I get my bag, okay?

1454
01:14:10,151 --> 01:14:11,252
Just stay there.

1455
01:14:11,352 --> 01:14:13,054
[Kyle breathes shakily]

1456
01:14:13,154 --> 01:14:15,623
I'm fine. I'm fine.

1457
01:14:16,524 --> 01:14:18,192
What is that?

1458
01:14:21,896 --> 01:14:23,531
Oh.

1459
01:14:23,631 --> 01:14:26,567
Wow! Look at this. [chuckles]

1460
01:14:26,667 --> 01:14:31,672
Cards have been the undoing
of many a man.

1461
01:14:31,772 --> 01:14:33,374
But they spared you.

1462
01:14:33,473 --> 01:14:36,777
You are a lucky young man.

1463
01:14:36,877 --> 01:14:42,183
But you hurt your head, you see?

1464
01:14:42,516 --> 01:14:44,151
-[Kyle groaning]
-That's enough!

1465
01:14:44,251 --> 01:14:46,153
[Kyle continues groaning]

1466
01:14:48,556 --> 01:14:51,258
That's enough, that's enough.

1467
01:14:51,592 --> 01:14:53,427
Stop! Stop, stop! [cries]

1468
01:14:53,527 --> 01:14:56,564
No, this is just a warm-up,
you know?

1469
01:14:56,664 --> 01:14:59,000
A blowtorch, some rock salt...

1470
01:14:59,100 --> 01:15:00,701
By the time I am done,

1471
01:15:00,801 --> 01:15:03,503
your brother will thank me
for killing him!

1472
01:15:03,604 --> 01:15:07,608
Okay, okay. I'll go. I'll go.
Just stop.

1473
01:15:08,943 --> 01:15:11,512
[stammers]

1474
01:15:11,612 --> 01:15:14,281
It's funny. You know how...

1475
01:15:14,882 --> 01:15:21,622
a little well-placed brutality
can solve what talk never could.

1476
01:15:24,658 --> 01:15:26,160
[Logan] Look.
This mesh, it'll protect you

1477
01:15:26,260 --> 01:15:29,997
against the curious bite,
but not an attack, all right?

1478
01:15:30,097 --> 01:15:31,165
Should or will?

1479
01:15:31,265 --> 01:15:36,137
I've no idea. Never had
the guts to check it myself.

1480
01:15:36,637 --> 01:15:39,340
I'll be sure to put it
on my Yelp review.

1481
01:15:39,440 --> 01:15:42,176
You have a fresh tank
and a new BCD.

1482
01:15:42,276 --> 01:15:44,845
With the weight of the bag,
it'll take a while for you

1483
01:15:44,945 --> 01:15:47,281
to get back into the surface.

1484
01:15:50,885 --> 01:15:55,456
Anything comes near you,
go for the eyes. Got it?

1485
01:15:55,556 --> 01:15:56,991
Stay confident.

1486
01:15:57,091 --> 01:16:01,128
Turn to face the shark
and don't break eye contact.

1487
01:16:01,462 --> 01:16:03,898
Sharks rely on the element
of surprise.

1488
01:16:04,331 --> 01:16:08,602
Facing them shows awareness.
They don't like it.

1489
01:16:10,037 --> 01:16:11,639
You got this.

1490
01:16:15,643 --> 01:16:17,344
I'll come back for you guys.

1491
01:16:18,479 --> 01:16:20,347
I'll take care of them.
Don't worry.

1492
01:16:34,328 --> 01:16:36,030
[air hissing]

1493
01:16:49,443 --> 01:16:51,212
Shark mesh, huh?

1494
01:16:53,214 --> 01:16:55,216
It won't help.

1495
01:17:08,395 --> 01:17:09,598
God.

1496
01:17:09,697 --> 01:17:12,133
Where is it?

1497
01:17:12,567 --> 01:17:14,068
Come on.

1498
01:17:16,971 --> 01:17:18,205
Okay.

1499
01:17:21,342 --> 01:17:23,277
[ominous music playing]

1500
01:17:23,377 --> 01:17:26,013
[breathes shakily]

1501
01:17:26,113 --> 01:17:27,348
Fuck.

1502
01:17:35,524 --> 01:17:38,058
Not today, you ugly bastard.

1503
01:17:46,333 --> 01:17:48,302
[humming]

1504
01:17:56,611 --> 01:17:58,045
You okay, kid?

1505
01:17:59,847 --> 01:18:01,849
-Better.
-Good.

1506
01:18:01,949 --> 01:18:05,286
You keep talking to her
and keep her warm, all right?

1507
01:18:05,386 --> 01:18:08,422
We're gonna be fine
if we do what we're told.

1508
01:18:08,523 --> 01:18:10,090
You want something?

1509
01:18:12,893 --> 01:18:15,763
[softly]
Now, you take the knife.

1510
01:18:15,863 --> 01:18:16,830
[stammering] I can't.

1511
01:18:16,931 --> 01:18:19,534
Shit. Okay, okay. Fine.

1512
01:18:19,634 --> 01:18:21,302
[Logan]
You'll know when to use it.

1513
01:18:21,402 --> 01:18:23,237
Okay. Okay.

1514
01:18:35,983 --> 01:18:38,485
[footsteps departing]

1515
01:19:17,726 --> 01:19:20,629
[sobbing] I'm so sorry, TJ.

1516
01:19:20,995 --> 01:19:25,065
I'm just... so sorry.

1517
01:19:25,165 --> 01:19:27,134
[sobbing]

1518
01:19:34,808 --> 01:19:37,111
[continues sobbing]

1519
01:19:41,782 --> 01:19:43,951
[wailing]

1520
01:19:46,755 --> 01:19:48,889
[continues wailing]

1521
01:20:01,268 --> 01:20:02,469
Goodbye.

1522
01:20:06,407 --> 01:20:08,809
[breathes shakily]

1523
01:20:09,243 --> 01:20:10,578
[exhales]

1524
01:20:18,118 --> 01:20:19,153
Okay.

1525
01:20:32,166 --> 01:20:34,201
I've got the bag. I'm headed up.

1526
01:20:34,301 --> 01:20:37,605
<i>Sorry for the delay.</i>
<i>I got caught up.</i>

1527
01:20:40,307 --> 01:20:43,578
Good girl.
We will worry about you.

1528
01:20:45,079 --> 01:20:48,315
Well, this day's really
starting to turn around,

1529
01:20:48,415 --> 01:20:51,051
isn't it, <i>Capitán?</i>

1530
01:21:05,533 --> 01:21:07,034
No...

1531
01:21:07,769 --> 01:21:10,705
No. [breathes shakily]

1532
01:21:10,805 --> 01:21:13,340
[yelling]

1533
01:21:16,845 --> 01:21:18,613
Stay away! [groans]

1534
01:21:24,552 --> 01:21:25,653
Okay.

1535
01:21:27,020 --> 01:21:29,890
Okay. You want to mess with me?

1536
01:21:29,990 --> 01:21:31,959
Okay. [grunts]

1537
01:21:34,495 --> 01:21:36,063
Look at me.

1538
01:21:37,464 --> 01:21:38,533
Look at me.

1539
01:21:39,868 --> 01:21:43,404
-[roars]
-[screams]

1540
01:21:43,504 --> 01:21:45,573
[grunting]

1541
01:21:52,446 --> 01:21:54,516
[yelling]

1542
01:21:54,616 --> 01:21:56,651
[panting]

1543
01:21:57,886 --> 01:22:00,120
[breathing shakily]

1544
01:22:04,559 --> 01:22:05,959
[sighs]

1545
01:22:06,460 --> 01:22:08,028
[gasps]

1546
01:22:08,128 --> 01:22:12,299
You've gotta be kidding me.
[panting]

1547
01:22:12,399 --> 01:22:14,368
Shit! Shit! Shit!

1548
01:22:23,711 --> 01:22:25,045
[roars]

1549
01:22:30,017 --> 01:22:31,285
There.

1550
01:22:31,385 --> 01:22:36,089
I can do this. [panting]
I can do this.

1551
01:22:44,431 --> 01:22:46,233
I'm gonna make this
right for you.

1552
01:22:47,669 --> 01:22:49,537
[groaning]

1553
01:22:53,273 --> 01:22:55,577
-[heroic music playing]
-[breathes relieved]

1554
01:22:57,946 --> 01:22:59,213
I got the bag!

1555
01:22:59,948 --> 01:23:01,215
There she is.

1556
01:23:01,315 --> 01:23:04,418
If you want this,
you're gonna have to help me.

1557
01:23:04,519 --> 01:23:05,486
Tatiana!

1558
01:23:10,925 --> 01:23:13,761
Amazing, Tatiana! Bring her up.

1559
01:23:15,597 --> 01:23:18,633
Garrison!
Come on, man, move your ass!

1560
01:23:20,902 --> 01:23:23,337
[Tatiana groans] Take it.

1561
01:23:23,771 --> 01:23:26,841
Take it. Just take it. [groans]

1562
01:23:26,941 --> 01:23:29,677
The bag. The bag.
The bag. The bag.

1563
01:23:30,210 --> 01:23:34,314
Just give me the goddamn bag.
Yeah.

1564
01:23:37,952 --> 01:23:40,487
Kyle! Is she okay?

1565
01:23:42,489 --> 01:23:46,293
Look at that. Wow, we did it.

1566
01:23:46,393 --> 01:23:49,864
For a moment I thought that this
was going to be impossible,

1567
01:23:49,964 --> 01:23:52,667
but here we are.

1568
01:23:52,767 --> 01:23:54,903
[exhales deeply]

1569
01:23:55,003 --> 01:23:57,070
-[sighs]
-[Tatiana] So...

1570
01:23:58,205 --> 01:24:00,407
You're gonna let us go, right?

1571
01:24:01,709 --> 01:24:04,311
Well, you completed
your end of the deal,

1572
01:24:05,013 --> 01:24:08,215
so I'll do as I said.

1573
01:24:12,119 --> 01:24:15,422
Logan, I'll be seeing you.

1574
01:24:15,523 --> 01:24:18,258
Garrison, I'll call you
when the new shipment is in.

1575
01:24:18,358 --> 01:24:19,393
And... [in Spanish]

1576
01:24:24,164 --> 01:24:26,701
[sucks teeth] Oh! Oh!

1577
01:24:26,801 --> 01:24:28,201
One more thing.

1578
01:24:29,169 --> 01:24:32,272
-I am lying.
-[suspenseful music playing]

1579
01:24:32,372 --> 01:24:33,440
Delgado.

1580
01:24:41,381 --> 01:24:43,785
-[grunts]
-[Delgado groans]

1581
01:24:48,388 --> 01:24:49,757
Oh!

1582
01:24:51,458 --> 01:24:52,594
[roars]

1583
01:24:54,629 --> 01:24:56,531
[breathes shakily]

1584
01:24:57,899 --> 01:24:59,534
[Burns groans]

1585
01:24:59,634 --> 01:25:00,702
No.

1586
01:25:02,737 --> 01:25:04,304
You know, I mean...

1587
01:25:04,404 --> 01:25:08,610
Boy, you've got balls,
and I respect that.

1588
01:25:08,710 --> 01:25:09,744
Fuck you!

1589
01:25:10,143 --> 01:25:12,614
Yeah, well, it doesn't change
what comes next.

1590
01:25:12,714 --> 01:25:13,815
Garrison, the gun.

1591
01:25:16,551 --> 01:25:17,451
Garrison!

1592
01:25:19,020 --> 01:25:20,420
-Sorry, boss.
-What?

1593
01:25:20,521 --> 01:25:23,091
I'm not gonna do that for you.

1594
01:25:23,190 --> 01:25:24,559
-Huh?
-You always say

1595
01:25:24,659 --> 01:25:27,327
it's about business,
it's not personal, right?

1596
01:25:27,427 --> 01:25:29,329
Well, this seems to be
fucking personal to me.

1597
01:25:29,429 --> 01:25:31,933
So the gun stays with me.

1598
01:25:32,299 --> 01:25:34,468
It's nice you've been listening
to me.

1599
01:25:34,569 --> 01:25:36,638
But if you have been listening
to me,

1600
01:25:36,738 --> 01:25:40,675
you probably heard me saying,
"No loose ends!"

1601
01:25:42,242 --> 01:25:44,112
[Burns muttering]

1602
01:25:44,211 --> 01:25:47,180
You know? [sighs]
It's okay. Because...

1603
01:25:47,749 --> 01:25:50,652
I made my first killing
with a knife.

1604
01:25:55,823 --> 01:25:56,758
[grunts]

1605
01:25:57,091 --> 01:25:58,325
You stole my life.

1606
01:25:58,425 --> 01:26:03,230
Your good-for-nothing
son's habit stole your life.

1607
01:26:03,330 --> 01:26:07,535
I gave you an option,
so I didn't have to take his.

1608
01:26:07,635 --> 01:26:08,636
[gunshots]

1609
01:26:08,736 --> 01:26:10,071
[Burns groans]

1610
01:26:10,538 --> 01:26:12,073
I think it's time
you take your bag...

1611
01:26:12,172 --> 01:26:15,208
-[Burns] Hey, hey.
-...and get off this boat.

1612
01:26:15,308 --> 01:26:16,944
-Hey...
-Listen to me,

1613
01:26:17,045 --> 01:26:19,212
you boomer motherfucker!

1614
01:26:19,647 --> 01:26:23,718
You murdered my friends,
injured my family

1615
01:26:23,818 --> 01:26:25,820
and ruined my vacation.

1616
01:26:25,920 --> 01:26:29,222
I should shoot you
where you stand right now.

1617
01:26:29,322 --> 01:26:32,325
And the only reason
you're still breathing

1618
01:26:32,426 --> 01:26:36,164
is because I'm choosing
to show restraint.

1619
01:26:36,263 --> 01:26:38,198
You're done here.

1620
01:26:38,298 --> 01:26:41,803
Off this boat. Now!

1621
01:26:43,071 --> 01:26:46,373
Before I change my fucking mind.

1622
01:26:49,043 --> 01:26:50,444
You know?

1623
01:26:51,512 --> 01:26:54,347
I think I'm on my way out
after all.

1624
01:26:54,448 --> 01:26:59,987
But, trust me, this is most
definitely not the end.

1625
01:27:06,861 --> 01:27:09,229
I'll be seeing you.

1626
01:27:09,329 --> 01:27:13,266
Especially you, Tatiana.

1627
01:27:25,980 --> 01:27:28,716
[panting]

1628
01:27:28,816 --> 01:27:30,685
[soft music playing]

1629
01:27:49,203 --> 01:27:51,371
[engine starts]

1630
01:27:59,547 --> 01:28:01,481
Hey, are you okay?

1631
01:28:04,152 --> 01:28:05,887
Are you okay?

1632
01:28:05,987 --> 01:28:08,488
No. Are you?

1633
01:28:10,057 --> 01:28:13,895
You don't get to play games
with your life anymore, okay?

1634
01:28:14,262 --> 01:28:16,429
Because,
whether you like it or not,

1635
01:28:16,531 --> 01:28:18,533
I'm in this with you, too.

1636
01:28:18,633 --> 01:28:20,768
I don't plan on it. [sniffles]

1637
01:28:22,270 --> 01:28:23,971
[Kyle sighs]

1638
01:28:27,241 --> 01:28:29,277
Is he gonna come after us?

1639
01:28:29,376 --> 01:28:30,745
Absolutely.

1640
01:28:35,049 --> 01:28:36,584
Why'd you help us?

1641
01:28:38,351 --> 01:28:39,754
Anyone that went through

1642
01:28:39,854 --> 01:28:41,556
what you went through
deserves to walk away.

1643
01:28:41,656 --> 01:28:44,258
He should have kept
his end of the bargain.

1644
01:28:44,357 --> 01:28:47,562
I thought
he was a man of principle.

1645
01:28:47,662 --> 01:28:49,597
Turns out
he was just batshit crazy.

1646
01:28:49,697 --> 01:28:50,832
[scoffs]

1647
01:28:51,398 --> 01:28:52,533
[chuckles]

1648
01:29:26,499 --> 01:29:28,102
[flare whistles]

1649
01:29:30,238 --> 01:29:33,440
-Shit!
-[flare continues whistling]

1650
01:29:39,914 --> 01:29:41,381
[gasps]

1651
01:29:51,225 --> 01:29:52,593
[gasps]

1652
01:29:57,397 --> 01:29:59,867
For emergencies.

1653
01:29:59,967 --> 01:30:02,536
And that was certainly
an emergency.

1654
01:30:02,637 --> 01:30:05,339
That's what you were doing
when you checked the fuel.

1655
01:30:05,438 --> 01:30:07,909
What if I'd gone on the boat?

1656
01:30:08,342 --> 01:30:10,477
I wouldn't have done that,
would I?

1657
01:30:13,047 --> 01:30:15,182
Get us a drink.

1658
01:30:16,483 --> 01:30:18,719
Let's get you three
to the hospital.

1659
01:30:19,387 --> 01:30:21,589
-Thank you, Captain.
-[Kayle and Logan groan]

1660
01:30:21,689 --> 01:30:24,158
-[Kayle groans]
-Okay. Hey.

1661
01:30:24,258 --> 01:30:26,694
Keep it elevated, all right?

1662
01:30:27,395 --> 01:30:28,729
[softly] All right.

1663
01:30:37,972 --> 01:30:39,240
[exhales]

1664
01:30:39,340 --> 01:30:41,042
Did I ever tell you
about the Irish

1665
01:30:41,142 --> 01:30:44,111
-who fought at the Alamo?
-I don't think so.

1666
01:30:44,211 --> 01:30:48,849
Well, they were so badly treated
by their own gang,

1667
01:30:48,950 --> 01:30:51,252
they switched sides
and joined the Mexican army.

1668
01:30:51,352 --> 01:30:53,821
[sighs] Oh my God.

1669
01:30:54,588 --> 01:30:55,957
[chuckles]

1670
01:30:57,191 --> 01:30:58,292
[sighs]

1671
01:30:58,392 --> 01:31:00,628
[melancholic music playing]

1672
01:31:13,441 --> 01:31:15,176
[music fades out]

1673
01:31:18,446 --> 01:31:21,481
[downtempo music playing]

1674
01:34:19,393 --> 01:34:21,362
[tense music playing]

1675
01:35:30,565 --> 01:35:31,732
[music ends]